A thread woken from a notification keeps naming it.
Only a waiting thread names a notification;
a ready one that still does breaks the thread-state invariant.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: runnable thread waits on something

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -63,3 +63,2 @@ static void unwait(struct thread *t)
     ring_remove(&((struct notification *)p2v(t->waiting_on))->waiters, t);
-    t->waiting_on = 0;
 }
